---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who writes LingoGrove and what it covers: translations, loanword meanings, verb conjugations, and grammar for English speakers."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] md:text-4xl">About LingoGrove</h1>

		<div class="mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p class="mb-4">
				LingoGrove is a reference site for English speakers who hit a specific word or phrase in
				another language and need a straight answer: what it means, how to say it, how a verb
				conjugates, or which of two similar words actually fits. It is not a course. There is no
				sign-up, no streak to keep, no lesson plan. You look something up, you get a real answer
				with the nuance that matters (which region uses it, how formal it is, what a dictionary
				you can check for yourself actually says), and you leave.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Every translation and word meaning is checked against a standard dictionary for that
				language rather than written from memory. Verb conjugation tables are generated by code
				and checked against a published grammar reference, not typed in by hand, for the same
				reason a calculator site double-checks its formulas: a wrong answer here is the kind of
				mistake a reader only discovers after they have already used it in an email or an
				assignment.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4 text-[var(--ink)]">
				This site is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}.
			</p>
			<p class="m-0 text-[var(--ink)]">
				Questions, corrections, or press inquiries:
				<a href="mailto:contact@lingogrove.com" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline">contact@lingogrove.com</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
